The MCP server now offers tools to read, create, change, delete and publish forms, and to read and change the editorial guidelines of a node. External forms can be read, but not changed. The server no longer lets a caller remove their own account from a group. The MCP tools search_content, count_content and find_similar moved to the enterprise modules, so a server without them does not list these tools. The MCP tool create_user no longer takes a password: the new user sets it on a one-time link, and the tool returns only the link's expiry.
